# Chaos: the helper's cooldown channels (Lua only; applies after 0001-0061; server/README.md "Cooldown channels").
# Owner, 2026-10-16: heal and attack must never wait for each other. The server keeps a channel per kind of action
# (engine src-patch 0042: attack spells and runes, healing spells and runes, potions, moves) and the auto attack never
# waits for any; the helper still serialised them in the client:
# - one rate guard for every spell cast (0026: at most 4 a second, all kinds together): the attack rotation used up the
#   second and the heal waited. Now each cast channel (heal, attack, support; overlay game_helpertimers,
#   ChaosHelperTimers) has its own guard of the same size: healing spells and the friend heals use "heal", the magic
#   shooter the channel of the spell's group, the rest "support".
# - one object-use timer (multiUseExDelay, 1 s) for potions, the healing rune, the shooter's runes and special foods,
#   plus a potion "turn" that kept the next potion back 1.1 s after every rune: an attack rune held the health potion.
#   Now potion, healRune, attackRune, supportRune and food each have their own timer (a rune by its group).
# - a heal waited while a cast-time attack spell charged (0052: the server interrupted the cast on any other spell).
#   The server interrupts it only on another attack spell or rune now (data/lib/chaos_casting.lua), so the heal goes
#   out at once; the shooter still waits with attack spells and attack runes, no longer with support spells.
# Without the overlay module the old shared guard and timer stay. Tests: overlay game_helpertimers/helpertimers_test.lua.
